sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch11-18> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Rule 110 and its reflections are the only clear elementary class 4 rules" ;
    dct:description "Among the 256 elementary cellular automata, the only clear immediate example of class 4 behavior is rule 110 together with its left-right and black-white equivalents (rules 124, 137 and 193), while class 4 behavior is common once more colors or neighbors are allowed, even for totalistic rules." ;
    delphi:context "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 11, “The Notion of Computation”; section “Class 4 Behavior and Universality” (from p. 691), p. 693. Scope: the 256 elementary cellular automata and multi-color or larger-neighborhood rules" ;
    dct:type "computational-observation" .
}

